    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW266b2wAzfAJMBjD5JpGuLWE)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent; fixes the toggle from #529 and #530 (both merged).\n\n## What was wrong\n\n- Caps+x switched highlighting off by looking for a menu item starting with \"Select\", \"Pointer\" or \"Text Selection\". DEVONthink's tool that selects text is called just \"Text\", so none matched.\n- With no match, the code chose \"Highlight Text\" again, which does not turn highlighting off. It still showed the \"Select\" alert, which is exactly what Sia saw: the alert, and nothing happening.\n\n## What changes\n\n- The exact title \"Text\" is tried first (`^Text$`, so it never matches \"Highlight Text\" or \"Text Note\"), then the old patterns.\n- If there is no Text tool, an alert says so and nothing changes, instead of choosing Highlight Text again.\n- The alert after switching off now says \"Text\".\n\n## Not verified (no Mac or DEVONthink here)\n\n- That the menu item is exactly \"Text\" and sits in Tools > Annotate. If the alert says \"No Text tool in Tools > Annotate\", run `DEVONthink.dumpMenu(\"Tools\")` and send me the Annotate part.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Reload Hammerspoon: no error in the console.\n- [ ] Open a PDF, press Caps+x: the alert says \"Highlight\" and highlighting works.\n- [ ] Press Caps+x again: the alert says \"Text\" and you can select text normally.\n- [ ] Repeat a few times: it keeps switching in both directions.\n- [ ] Caps+c, the colour keys, Cmd+Z and Cmd+Shift+Z still work.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCTb5QFPFZUd9wzRgq)_",
